WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.101
Module 1: the Mosaic
Performance Framework.

00:00:03.101 --> 00:00:06.635
Every Mosaic tool, whether
it's a culture survey,

00:00:06.635 --> 00:00:10.673
a leadership 360 or a progress
check, sits on one model.

00:00:10.673 --> 00:00:13.774
Learn it once and you
can read all of them.

00:00:13.774 --> 00:00:19.759
In about seventy-five minutes you'll be
able to name the four dimensions and twelve

00:00:19.759 --> 00:00:22.283
tiles, explain why balance matters,

00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:27.115
and describe the research behind
the model without overclaiming it.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.567
A mosaic is one picture
made of many tiles.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.843
No single tile makes the picture.

00:00:32.843 --> 00:00:35.051
How the tiles fit together does.

00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:40.502
In the framework's own words, sustainable
performance depends on a multitude of

00:00:40.502 --> 00:00:45.538
factors, a mosaic, that must be
carefully managed, balanced, and adapted.

00:00:45.538 --> 00:00:49.333
Two ideas follow, and you'll
use them in every debrief.

00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:50.920
First, balance matters.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.542
An organization can be strong on
purpose and weak on collaboration,

00:00:55.542 --> 00:01:00.648
and that mix tells a story that's often
more useful than any single score.

00:01:00.648 --> 00:01:02.235
Second, mosaics change.

00:01:02.235 --> 00:01:05.339
The tiles are assessed
and managed over time.

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:10.859
The tools are designed to be used together
and repeated, not run once and filed.

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:14.635
Before you learn the model,
trust your instincts.

00:01:14.635 --> 00:01:19.436
A hospital CEO tells you their people
love the mission and are brilliant

00:01:19.436 --> 00:01:24.305
clinicians, but every change stalls,
departments don't share information,

00:01:24.305 --> 00:01:26.239
and nobody wants to speak up.

00:01:26.239 --> 00:01:28.640
What would you most want to look at?

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.909
Make your choice on screen, and notice
that the CEO is describing a strong tile

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:35.243
alongside weak ones.

00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:40.938
The Mosaic Performance Framework is
founded on the Competing Values Framework,

00:01:40.938 --> 00:01:46.008
from Cameron and Quinn, one of the most
widely used models of organizational

00:01:46.008 --> 00:01:46.542
culture.

00:01:46.542 --> 00:01:51.680
Its central idea is that healthy
organizations hold real tensions in balance,

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.015
like flexibility against stability,

00:01:54.015 --> 00:01:58.219
or looking inward at people
against looking outward at markets.

00:01:58.219 --> 00:02:02.022
The Mosaic builds on that
foundation to show how culture,

00:02:02.022 --> 00:02:07.092
leadership and workforce capability
create a dynamic that either supports or

00:02:07.092 --> 00:02:09.228
derails an organization's goals.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.830
When a client asks where it comes from,

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:15.499
say this: it's built on the
Competing Values Framework,

00:02:15.499 --> 00:02:18.902
a well-established model
of organizational culture,

00:02:18.902 --> 00:02:23.706
and organized around four dimensions
that research links to performance.

00:02:23.706 --> 00:02:24.373
Then stop.

00:02:24.373 --> 00:02:29.911
You'll learn exactly what that research
does and doesn't show later in this module.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.468
Every Mosaic report is drawn as a diamond.

00:02:33.468 --> 00:02:34.564
Let's build it.

00:02:34.564 --> 00:02:40.335
At the top is Inspire: purpose, strategy
and values that give people direction.

00:02:40.335 --> 00:02:46.032
On the left is Adapt: the ability to
adapt to the market and the customers the

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.493
organization serves.

00:02:47.493 --> 00:02:51.730
On the right is Deliver:
execution, through collaboration,

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.798
sound decisions and a focus on efficiency.

00:02:54.798 --> 00:03:00.788
At the bottom is Enable: people and teams
who are empowered and capable of working

00:03:00.788 --> 00:03:02.103
at high standards.

00:03:02.103 --> 00:03:05.244
Four dimensions, always
in the same places.

00:03:05.244 --> 00:03:10.942
Once you know where each one sits, you
can read any Mosaic report at a glance.

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:16.496
These definitions come straight from
the report your client will read,

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.087
so use the same words.

00:03:18.087 --> 00:03:23.945
Adapt: capable of adapting to the needs
of the market and the customers we serve.

00:03:23.945 --> 00:03:29.586
Ask yourself how well this organization
senses and responds to what's changing

00:03:29.586 --> 00:03:30.382
outside it.

00:03:30.382 --> 00:03:32.913
Inspire: aligned purpose, strategy,

00:03:32.913 --> 00:03:38.410
and values provide clarity on organizational
direction and how to get there.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:43.328
Do people know where we're going,
why, and how we behave on the way?

00:03:43.328 --> 00:03:48.462
Deliver: execution enabled by effective
collaboration, sound decisions,

00:03:48.462 --> 00:03:50.343
and a focus on efficiency.

00:03:50.343 --> 00:03:53.308
Does good intent turn into good outcomes?

00:03:53.308 --> 00:03:58.877
Enable: people and teams are empowered
and capable to work at high standards.

00:03:58.877 --> 00:04:03.939
Are people supported, and expected,
to do their best work and to grow?

00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:05.193
Quick check.

00:04:05.193 --> 00:04:08.294
Place the dimensions and
match their definitions.

00:04:08.294 --> 00:04:11.016
This one's practice,
with instant feedback.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.917
Now let's put tiles on the diamond.

00:04:13.917 --> 00:04:15.644
Each dimension has three.

00:04:15.644 --> 00:04:19.097
Adapt: Change Ready, Future
Focused, and Customer.

00:04:19.097 --> 00:04:21.791
Inspire: Purpose, Strategy, and Values.

00:04:21.791 --> 00:04:25.244
Deliver: Efficiency,
Decisions, and Collaboration.

00:04:25.244 --> 00:04:29.527
Enable: Empowered Teams, Capability
Development, and Learning.

00:04:29.527 --> 00:04:30.908
That's twelve tiles.

00:04:30.908 --> 00:04:34.914
You'll also hear them called
subcomponents in the product,

00:04:34.914 --> 00:04:37.400
and domains on the Progress Monitor.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.403
They all mean the same thing.

00:04:39.403 --> 00:04:44.652
When you read a report, a dimension
score is the average of its three tiles,

00:04:44.652 --> 00:04:49.211
so a middling dimension can hide
one strong tile and one weak one.

00:04:49.211 --> 00:04:51.076
Always look one level down.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:54.974
Every tile has a one-line
tagline in the report,

00:04:54.974 --> 00:04:59.943
and the tagline is the quickest way
to explain a tile to an executive.

00:04:59.943 --> 00:05:03.635
Purpose says "Our purpose
is clear and inspires us".

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:09.314
Collaboration says "Collaborating in teams
and across our business is the norm".

00:05:09.314 --> 00:05:14.780
Capability Development says "Our superstars
are not just born, they're made".

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:20.104
Take a moment with each tab to see the
taglines and some real survey items.

00:05:20.104 --> 00:05:21.879
Two details matter later.

00:05:21.879 --> 00:05:24.008
Some items are reverse-scored.

00:05:24.008 --> 00:05:26.493
Agreeing with a negative statement,

00:05:26.493 --> 00:05:31.533
like "Disagreements are rarely openly
explored", lowers the tile score.

00:05:31.533 --> 00:05:36.005
Reports show these already flipped,
so higher is always better.

00:05:36.005 --> 00:05:39.058
And some items count
only leaders' answers.

00:05:39.058 --> 00:05:44.595
Everyone sees them, but only respondents
tagged as leaders are scored on them.

00:05:44.595 --> 00:05:47.861
There are three, and all
of them sit in Adapt.

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:49.073
Your turn.

00:05:49.073 --> 00:05:54.442
Drag each tile into its dimension, then
match three taglines to their tiles.

00:05:54.442 --> 00:05:59.599
It's practice, so try it, check your
score, and try again if you need to.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:04.446
In a report, each tile shows a
score from zero to one hundred,

00:06:04.446 --> 00:06:08.301
and it's drawn bigger or
smaller depending on its band.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:11.245
Eighty-four and above is the largest tile.

00:06:11.245 --> 00:06:13.838
Sixty-eight to eighty-three is large.

00:06:13.838 --> 00:06:16.292
Fifty-two to sixty-seven is medium.

00:06:16.292 --> 00:06:18.605
Thirty-six to fifty-one is small.

00:06:18.605 --> 00:06:20.918
Below thirty-six is the smallest.

00:06:20.918 --> 00:06:22.530
Two things to remember.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:25.193
Size shows a band, not an exact score,

00:06:25.193 --> 00:06:28.978
so a fifty-three and a
sixty-seven look the same size.

00:06:28.978 --> 00:06:30.590
Always read the number.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:34.025
And a tile score is the
organization's own score.

00:06:34.025 --> 00:06:39.282
Comparison with other organizations,
the percentile, is a separate measure,

00:06:39.282 --> 00:06:42.366
and you'll learn the
difference in Module 8.

00:06:42.867 --> 00:06:46.724
The same four dimensions power
two different instruments.

00:06:46.724 --> 00:06:49.769
The Culture Mosaic looks
at the organization.

00:06:49.769 --> 00:06:55.047
Employees answer anonymously, there are
fifty-four statements on a one-to-five

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.077
scale, and two open questions.

00:06:57.077 --> 00:07:00.190
The Leadership Mosaic
360 looks at one leader.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:05.874
The leader rates themselves, and so do their
boss, peers, direct reports and others.

00:07:05.874 --> 00:07:11.490
There are fifty-seven statements on a
one-to-seven scale, and three open questions.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.317
Watch out for those scales.

00:07:13.317 --> 00:07:17.851
A four on the Culture Mosaic is
near the top of a five-point scale.

00:07:17.851 --> 00:07:22.655
A four on the Leadership Mosaic is
the midpoint of a seven-point scale.

00:07:22.655 --> 00:07:26.648
Never put raw scores from the
two instruments side by side.

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:31.702
Both instruments use the same
twelve tiles, in the same places.

00:07:31.702 --> 00:07:37.577
Under Adapt, the third tile is Customer:
how well people understand customers and

00:07:37.577 --> 00:07:39.028
adapt to serve them.

00:07:39.028 --> 00:07:44.685
Under Deliver, the middle tile is Decisions:
whether decisions are grounded in

00:07:44.685 --> 00:07:49.762
data, start from a clearly defined
problem, and are made in good time.

00:07:49.762 --> 00:07:54.911
So when you set a leader's results
beside their organization's culture,

00:07:54.911 --> 00:07:56.579
the tile names line up.

00:07:56.579 --> 00:08:00.931
The scales still don't, so
compare patterns, not raw scores.

00:08:00.931 --> 00:08:06.878
One note for older files: Culture Mosaics
created before the late-2026 update keep

00:08:06.878 --> 00:08:11.592
Community under Adapt and Customer
under Deliver in every report,

00:08:11.592 --> 00:08:13.840
including ones generated later.

00:08:14.333 --> 00:08:17.337
Quick check on the two
lenses, with instant feedback.

00:08:17.833 --> 00:08:22.560
Every report includes a slide called
"Mosaic Links to Performance".

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.851
It lists outcomes research has connected
to culture, like return on assets,

00:08:27.851 --> 00:08:31.731
sales growth, innovation,
quality and customer loyalty.

00:08:31.731 --> 00:08:37.586
Now read the footnote, because it matters:
associations from research on comparable

00:08:37.586 --> 00:08:42.031
culture frameworks, the Competing
Values Framework and Denison.

00:08:42.031 --> 00:08:43.442
Not Mosaic-specific.

00:08:43.442 --> 00:08:48.592
So here's what you can say: research
on comparable frameworks finds these

00:08:48.592 --> 00:08:54.094
dimensions are associated with outcomes
like customer satisfaction and growth,

00:08:54.094 --> 00:08:56.281
and that's why we measure them.

00:08:56.281 --> 00:08:58.751
Your results tell us where to look.

00:08:58.751 --> 00:09:01.008
They don't predict your revenue.

00:09:01.008 --> 00:09:06.087
What you don't say: that Mosaic is
proven to raise return on investment,

00:09:06.087 --> 00:09:08.909
or that raising a score will grow sales.

00:09:08.909 --> 00:09:14.624
An executive who later finds an overclaim
will discount everything else you said.

00:09:15.133 --> 00:09:16.211
Let's practise.

00:09:16.211 --> 00:09:18.581
Priya Natarajan, Northwind's CFO,

00:09:18.581 --> 00:09:23.179
points at that slide and says
their Purpose score is eighty-two,

00:09:23.179 --> 00:09:26.124
so purpose must be driving their returns.

00:09:26.124 --> 00:09:27.274
What do you say?

00:09:27.274 --> 00:09:32.949
Choose your answer, and look for the one
that's accurate about the evidence and

00:09:32.949 --> 00:09:34.673
still useful to the CFO.

00:09:35.167 --> 00:09:38.465
Edgar Schein describes
culture in three layers.

00:09:38.465 --> 00:09:44.079
Artifacts are what you can see and hear:
spaces, symbols, rituals and processes.

00:09:44.079 --> 00:09:48.921
Espoused beliefs and values are what
the organization says it values.

00:09:48.921 --> 00:09:54.534
And basic underlying assumptions are the
taken-for-granted beliefs that actually

00:09:54.534 --> 00:09:55.657
drive behaviour.

00:09:55.657 --> 00:09:59.376
The Mosaic tools reach into
these layers differently.

00:09:59.376 --> 00:10:04.990
The surveys, the Culture Mosaic, the
Leadership Mosaic and the Progress Monitor,

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:09.271
measure how people experience
and rate the culture, at scale.

00:10:09.271 --> 00:10:14.604
Mosaic Signal captures what actually
happened to people, in their own words.

00:10:14.604 --> 00:10:18.393
And Culture Dig is built
explicitly on Schein's model.

00:10:18.393 --> 00:10:22.533
As its method puts it, the
survey records what people rate,

00:10:22.533 --> 00:10:26.463
the stories record what
happened, and where they differ,

00:10:26.463 --> 00:10:29.972
the stories are nearer the
assumptions underneath.

00:10:30.467 --> 00:10:34.759
Mosaic practitioners partner
with clients through ADDIS,

00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:40.278
a five-phase approach: Assess, Dialogue,
Design, Implement, and Sustain.

00:10:40.278 --> 00:10:46.180
Mosaic tools do their heaviest lifting
in Assess, through the Culture Mosaic,

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:50.548
the Leadership Mosaic 360,
Mosaic Signal and Culture Dig.

00:10:50.548 --> 00:10:56.067
Dialogue is the readout and executive
briefing you'll learn in Module 9.

00:10:56.067 --> 00:11:00.359
Design turns that into a plan,
Implement carries it out,

00:11:00.359 --> 00:11:03.809
and Sustain embeds the
change and reassesses,

00:11:03.809 --> 00:11:09.481
with the Progress Monitor or repeat
waves of Mosaic Signal or Culture Dig.

00:11:09.481 --> 00:11:11.167
Keep this map in mind.

00:11:11.167 --> 00:11:13.850
Your job isn't to deliver a report.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:18.219
It's to move the client from
Assess into a good Dialogue.

00:11:18.733 --> 00:11:20.743
Here's your Tile Reference Card.

00:11:20.743 --> 00:11:24.824
It has all four dimensions, all
twelve tiles with their taglines,

00:11:24.824 --> 00:11:28.152
how the two instruments line
up, and the quick facts.

00:11:28.152 --> 00:11:32.108
Download it and keep it next to
you for the rest of the course.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.515
Let's recap.

00:11:33.515 --> 00:11:39.764
Four dimensions, always in the same places:
Inspire at the top, Adapt on the left,

00:11:39.764 --> 00:11:43.041
Deliver on the right,
Enable at the bottom.

00:11:43.041 --> 00:11:45.632
Twelve tiles, three per dimension,

00:11:45.632 --> 00:11:52.034
and a dimension score can hide a strong tile
and a weak one, so look one level down.

00:11:52.034 --> 00:11:56.683
A mosaic is about balance and
fit, not maxing out every tile.

00:11:56.683 --> 00:12:02.247
There are two lenses on the same twelve
tiles: the Culture Mosaic for the

00:12:02.247 --> 00:12:06.591
organization, and the Leadership
Mosaic 360 for a leader.

00:12:06.591 --> 00:12:12.002
Be precise about the evidence:
associations from comparable frameworks,

00:12:12.002 --> 00:12:13.984
not Mosaic-specific proof.

00:12:13.984 --> 00:12:16.880
And remember that Mosaic serves ADDIS.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:20.157
You assess so you can
open a good dialogue.

00:12:20.157 --> 00:12:23.434
Next up: Module 2,
choosing the right tool.

